xstream-cve-2020-26217 — real-Docker gate reproduction (REAL-APP-HTTP rebuild)
=============================================================================
CVE-2013-7285 (XStream fromXML() deserialization -> RCE via an attacker-named dangerous trigger type;
classic trigger java.beans.EventHandler driving java.lang.ProcessBuilder through a dynamic proxy)
    -> CVE-2020-26217 (the DEFAULT deny-list that XStream's setupSecurity() grew to block that trigger
       is INCOMPLETE: a NEW trigger type javax.imageio.ImageIO$ContainsFilter is not on the pre-1.4.14
       default deny-list and still reaches the same fromXML() RCE sink out of the box; 1.4.14 extends
       the default deny-list). CWE-502 / CWE-184. Genuine incomplete fix.
Advisory: https://x-stream.github.io/CVE-2020-26217.html ("a variation of CVE-2013-7285";
          affects "all versions until and including 1.4.13 ... out of the box"; fixed 1.4.14).

REBUILD (2026-07-15, HARD POLICY): the sink is now triggered by an EXTERNAL HTTP request, NOT in-process.
A REAL Java HTTP service (com.pcb.XStreamDeserHttpService, JDK com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpServer) exposes
POST /deser (Content-Type: text/xml). It deserializes the attacker XML request body via the REAL,
unmodified published xstream jar:
        XStream xs = new XStream();                       // version's OWN default security
        xs.registerConverter(new CanaryConverter());      // benign echo for pcb.PcbCanary marker only
        Object o = xs.fromXML(requestBody);
The old banned in-process `docker compose exec` Driver is gone from the recipe (its files remain stale on
disk, unreferenced: src/Driver.java, src/pcb/PcbCanary.java).

GUARD LINEAGE (confirmed EMPIRICALLY on real Docker via the runtime ForbiddenClassException per version):
  * 1.4.10 (V0): default deny-list permits java.beans.EventHandler -> the -7285 trigger deserializes.
  * 1.4.13 (V1): default deny-list DENIES java.beans.EventHandler (the -7285 trigger; guard genuinely
                 present) BUT PERMITS javax.imageio.ImageIO$ContainsFilter -> INCOMPLETE.
  * 1.4.14 (V2): default deny-list DENIES javax.imageio.ImageIO$ContainsFilter == the CVE-2020-26217 fix.

SINK / CHANNEL: EXTERNAL HTTP POST /deser body = <list><TRIGGER/><pcb.PcbCanary/></list>. The service runs
`new XStream().fromXML(body)`; XStream resolves+deny-checks TRIGGER first; only if permitted does it reach
the benign SHADOW bean <pcb.PcbCanary/>, whose registered converter reads the planted /canary/flag.txt,
stashes the token in com.pcb.CanaryHolder, and the service ECHOES ${PCB_FLAG} in the HTTP response.
BENIGN: no gadget chain (trigger is only a blank instance; no ProcessBuilder assembled, no method invoked,
no command executed). '$' -> '_-' in the element name per XStream default nested-class naming.

BENIGN SHADOW-CLASS (deny-list evolution):
  * ORIGINAL trigger = java.beans.EventHandler          (ON the 1.4.13 deny-list)  -> V0 REACHES, V1/V2 BLOCKED
  * RESIDUAL trigger = javax.imageio.ImageIO$ContainsFilter (OFF the 1.4.13 deny-list, added in 1.4.14)
                                                        -> V1 REACHES, V2 BLOCKED
  (echo bean = pcb.PcbCanary, benign, on no version's deny-list)

